---
// Article for the Small Text page (pt). The tool above it comes from SmallPage.
import SmallPage from '../../components/SmallPage.astro';
---

<SmallPage lang="pt">
  <article class="wrap max-w-[900px] mx-auto py-10 text-text">
    <!-- Styles -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-bold">Estilos de texto minúsculo para copiar e colar</h2>
      <p class="mb-5 leading-[1.8] text-text-muted">O texto pequeno também aparece como texto minúsculo ou fonte pequena. Para destacar suas bios, nomes de usuário e mensagens nas redes sociais, esses estilos de escrita se chamam sobrescrito, versaletes e subscrito.</p>
      <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="group rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-5 transition hover:border-primary hover:-translate-y-0.5">
          <span class="inline-block rounded-full bg-primary/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold text-primary">SS</span>
          <p class="mt-3 text-3xl leading-tight" dir="ltr">ᵗⁱⁿʸ</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-base font-semibold">Sobrescrito</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-text-muted leading-[1.6]">Letras minúsculas elevadas acima da linha.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="group rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-5 transition hover:border-primary hover:-translate-y-0.5">
          <span class="inline-block rounded-full bg-primary/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold text-primary">SC</span>
          <p class="mt-3 text-3xl leading-tight" dir="ltr">ᴛɪɴʏ</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-base font-semibold">Versaletes</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-text-muted leading-[1.6]">Maiúsculas em miniatura na altura das minúsculas.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="group rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-5 transition hover:border-primary hover:-translate-y-0.5">
          <span class="inline-block rounded-full bg-primary/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold text-primary">SB</span>
          <p class="mt-3 text-3xl leading-tight" dir="ltr">ₜᵢₙy</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-base font-semibold">Subscrito</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-text-muted leading-[1.6]">Letras minúsculas rebaixadas abaixo da linha.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How to -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold">Como usar o gerador de texto minúsculo</h2>
      <ol class="m-0 flex list-none flex-col gap-3 p-0">
        <li class="flex gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-4">
          <span class="flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary text-sm font-bold text-white">1</span>
          <p class="m-0 text-[.95rem] leading-[1.7]"><strong class="font-semibold">Digite seu texto.</strong> <span class="text-text-muted">Insira seu nome, bio ou qualquer frase na caixa acima para diminuir suas letras instantaneamente.</span></p>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-4">
          <span class="flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary text-sm font-bold text-white">2</span>
          <p class="m-0 text-[.95rem] leading-[1.7]"><strong class="font-semibold">Escolha um estilo minúsculo.</strong> <span class="text-text-muted">Escolha entre sobrescrito (ᵗⁱⁿʸ), subscrito (ₜᵢₙy) ou versaletes (ᴛɪɴʏ) para encontrar o visual em miniatura ideal.</span></p>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-4">
          <span class="flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary text-sm font-bold text-white">3</span>
          <p class="m-0 text-[.95rem] leading-[1.7]"><strong class="font-semibold">Copie e cole.</strong> <span class="text-text-muted">Clique no seu estilo favorito para copiá-lo.</span></p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- Alphabets -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-bold">Alfabeto do texto pequeno</h2>
      <p class="mb-5 leading-[1.8] text-text-muted">Para copiá-las, use SS, SC e SB respectivamente, como no exemplo abaixo:</p>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-5">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><span class="rounded-md bg-primary px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-white">SS</span><h3 class="text-base font-semibold">Sobrescrito (letras minúsculas elevadas)</h3></div>
        <p class="text-2xl leading-[1.9] break-words select-all tracking-wide" dir="ltr">ᵃ ᵇ ᶜ ᵈ ᵉ ᶠ ᵍ ʰ ⁱ ʲ ᵏ ˡ ᵐ ⁿ ᵒ ᵖ q ʳ ˢ ᵗ ᵘ ᵛ ʷ ˣ ʸ ᶻ</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-5">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><span class="rounded-md bg-primary px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-white">SC</span><h3 class="text-base font-semibold">Versaletes (maiúsculas em miniatura)</h3></div>
        <p class="text-2xl leading-[1.9] break-words select-all tracking-wide" dir="ltr">ᴀ ʙ ᴄ ᴅ ᴇ ꜰ ɢ ʜ ɪ ᴊ ᴋ ʟ ᴍ ɴ ᴏ ᴘ ǫ ʀ s ᴛ ᴜ ᴠ ᴡ x ʏ ᴢ</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-5">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><span class="rounded-md bg-primary px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-white">SB</span><h3 class="text-base font-semibold">Subscrito (letras minúsculas rebaixadas)</h3></div>
        <p class="text-2xl leading-[1.9] break-words select-all tracking-wide" dir="ltr">ₐ ₑ ₕ ᵢ ⱼ ₖ ₗ ₘ ₙ ₒ ₚ ᵣ ₛ ₜ ᵤ ᵥ ₓ</p>
        <p class="mt-3 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-primary bg-surface-2 px-3 py-2 text-sm leading-[1.6] text-text-muted"><strong class="text-text">Observação:</strong> O padrão Unicode não inclui letras subscritas nativas para b, c, d, f, g, q, w e z.</p>
      </div>
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-5">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><span class="rounded-md bg-primary px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-white">SS</span><h3 class="text-base font-semibold">Números sobrescritos</h3></div>
          <p class="text-2xl leading-[1.9] break-words select-all tracking-wide" dir="ltr">⁰ ¹ ² ³ ⁴ ⁵ ⁶ ⁷ ⁸ ⁹</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-5">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><span class="rounded-md bg-primary px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-white">SB</span><h3 class="text-base font-semibold">Números subscritos</h3></div>
          <p class="text-2xl leading-[1.9] break-words select-all tracking-wide" dir="ltr">₀ ₁ ₂ ₃ ₄ ₅ ₆ ₇ ₈ ₉</p>
        </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="mb-5 text-center text-2xl font-bold">Perguntas frequentes</h2>
      <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-[720px] flex-col gap-3">
      <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface px-5 py-4">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-[.95rem] font-medium">
          Posso usar esta fonte pequena no Facebook, Twitter, Tumblr e YouTube?
          <span class="shrink-0 text-text-muted transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[.9rem] leading-[1.7] text-text-muted">Sim, você pode usar essas letras pequenas no Facebook, Twitter (X), Tumblr e YouTube porque elas são feitas de símbolos Unicode universais.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface px-5 py-4">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-[.95rem] font-medium">
          Posso usar letras minúsculas no meu nome de usuário do Instagram?
          <span class="shrink-0 text-text-muted transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[.9rem] leading-[1.7] text-text-muted">Os nomes de usuário do Instagram só aceitam letras comuns, números, pontos e sublinhados, então símbolos Unicode não funcionam ali. Mas você pode usá-los livremente no campo Nome, na bio e nas legendas.</p>
      </details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</SmallPage>
